        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "51d51cda-80db-5135-873b-986a15ebd622",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Colocasia, Coronilla, Xanthosoma\n- Plant Families and Related Genera: Araceae, Caladium, Alocasia\n- Places: southeastern Asia, Indian subcontinent, Europe, North Africa\n- Topics: flowering plants, ornamental plants, common names\n\nFacts:\n- Colocasia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Araceae that is native to southeastern Asia and the Indian subcontinent.\n- Coronilla is a genus of about 20 species of flowering plants native to Europe and North Africa.\n- Xanthosoma includes species such as X. roseum that are used as ornamental plants.\n- In horticultural literature, Xanthosoma species are called ape or elephant ear because their leaves are said to resemble an elephant's ear.\n- The common name elephant ear is also sometimes applied to similar plants in the related genera Caladium, Colocasia, and Alocasia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d715b4d5-6220-5c81-b055-c8fa60252520",
        "text": "Page: Colocasia. Sentence: Colocasia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Araceae, native to southeastern Asia and the Indian subcontinent.\nPage: Coronilla. Sentence: The genus Coronilla contains about 20 species of flowering plants native to Europe and North Africa.\nPage: Xanthosoma. Sentence: Many other species (including especially \"X. roseum\") are used as ornamental plants, and in popular horticultural literature are known as ‘ape or elephant ear (from the purported resemblance of the leaf to an elephant's ear), although the latter name is sometimes also applied to members with similar appearance and uses in the closely related genera \"Caladium\", \"Colocasia\" (i.e., taro), and \"Alocasia\".",
